<title>USA: American Superconductor Q2 net loss rises.</title>
<headline>American Superconductor Q2 net loss rises.</headline>
<dateline>WESTBOROUGH, Mass. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months ended     Six months ended</p>
<p>			     September 30	    September 30</p>
<p>				1996	1995	 1996	 1995</p>
<p> Revenues	   $1,664,692 $1,598,630 $2,938,000 $2,603,338</p>
<p> Net loss	    2,396,788  1,858,701  5,670,841  3,914,338</p>
<p> Net loss per share     0.25	 0.20	 0.59	 0.41</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>			 9,561,551  9,469,244  9,559,520  9,468,940</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name of company is American Superconductor Corp.</p>
<p>For the three months ended September 30, 1996, in addition to reported revenues, American Superconductor Corp recorded $806,232 in funding under cost-sharing agreements versus $260,462 in the previous year's period. For the six-month period ended September 30, 1996, funding from cost-sharing agreements was $876,794 compared with $809,451 for the previous year's period.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
